1
00:00:23,808 --> 00:00:26,038
We're at the Incheon Munhak Stadium.

2
00:00:26,178 --> 00:00:30,008
I sometimes come to Incheon to film TV shows.

3
00:00:30,408 --> 00:00:33,648
Show directors love filming outdoors.

4
00:00:34,248 --> 00:00:35,447
- But the weather is indeed nice.
- So...

5
00:00:35,448 --> 00:00:37,118
- The weather is great.
- Yes.

6
00:00:37,788 --> 00:00:40,488
But hear me out. I film outdoors almost all week.

7
00:00:41,058 --> 00:00:43,858
As for them, they only film one show a week.

8
00:00:44,588 --> 00:00:45,958
That's the difference.

9
00:00:46,598 --> 00:00:47,858
I filmed outdoors yesterday.

10
00:00:49,528 --> 00:00:51,204
I'll film another show outdoors in two days.

11
00:00:51,228 --> 00:00:52,698
I never film inside a studio set.

12
00:00:52,998 --> 00:00:54,697
- I mostly film outdoors.
- You mostly film outdoors.

13
00:00:54,698 --> 00:00:57,138
Right. I've spent my whole life outdoors.

14
00:00:57,768 --> 00:00:59,907
As long as we're in the shade and away from the sun,

15
00:00:59,908 --> 00:01:01,837
- it's pretty cool.
- It's nice and cool.

16
00:01:01,838 --> 00:01:04,347
It's cool in the shade. It's indeed autumn now.

17
00:01:04,348 --> 00:01:05,447
- My gosh.
- I can feel it now.

18
00:01:05,448 --> 00:01:06,477
- Yes.
- Yes.

19
00:01:06,478 --> 00:01:08,747
- And the sky is very clear.
- Right.

20
00:01:08,748 --> 00:01:10,787
- The sky feels high too.
- Yes. It does.

21
00:01:10,788 --> 00:01:11,788
Right.

22
00:01:12,688 --> 00:01:13,758
Shall we go in?

23
00:01:14,288 --> 00:01:15,787
I guess we're all wearing red.

24
00:01:15,788 --> 00:01:17,257
Isn't that such an intense color?

25
00:01:17,258 --> 00:01:19,098
(Two men dressed in an intense shade of red)

26
00:01:19,558 --> 00:01:20,597
Games...

27
00:01:20,598 --> 00:01:22,568
(Even from behind, they look fierce.)

28
00:01:24,568 --> 00:01:26,138
Should I wave at them like this?

29
00:01:26,368 --> 00:01:28,138
- Are they filming us now?
- Here.

30
00:01:28,438 --> 00:01:29,468
I'm nervous.

31
00:01:29,838 --> 00:01:30,907
- You're nervous?
- Yes.

32
00:01:30,908 --> 00:01:31,937
Why?

33
00:01:31,938 --> 00:01:34,638
I'm going to meet Jae Seok in person.

34
00:01:35,138 --> 00:01:36,807
- Or they'd just curse.
- Right.

35
00:01:36,808 --> 00:01:38,408
- They wouldn't say hello.
- Who's that?

36
00:01:38,778 --> 00:01:39,818
I was right.

37
00:01:40,248 --> 00:01:41,968
- I was right.
- Was it really Byun Yo Han?

38
00:01:42,048 --> 00:01:43,947
- This was the intel you got.
- I was right. I...

39
00:01:43,948 --> 00:01:46,358
- Yes. It's for "Tazza." I told you.
- Oh, my.

40
00:01:46,418 --> 00:01:48,357
- I was right. It's Yo Han.
- Hello.

41
00:01:48,358 --> 00:01:49,658
- It was for "Tazza."
- Right.

42
00:01:49,828 --> 00:01:51,357
- Hello.
- "Tazza."

43
00:01:51,358 --> 00:01:53,657
- Gosh. Hello. Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

44
00:01:53,658 --> 00:01:54,897
Have you seen my works?

45
00:01:54,898 --> 00:01:55,928
Of course.

46
00:01:56,628 --> 00:01:58,928
(This new hire made a smooth entrance into the industry.)

47
00:01:59,638 --> 00:02:01,898
(As the early years of his acting career passed, )

48
00:02:02,368 --> 00:02:04,967
(he became the face of an era in "Mr. Sunshine.")

49
00:02:04,968 --> 00:02:07,408
(He was even showered with petals alongside a familiar face.)

50
00:02:08,038 --> 00:02:10,508
(He was fiercely dedicated to protect his country.)

51
00:02:10,808 --> 00:02:14,248
(Then he burned with passion to protect her too.)

52
00:02:14,818 --> 00:02:17,688
(Actor Byun Yo Han)

53
00:02:18,018 --> 00:02:20,688
(His performance as a villain was acknowledged by the world.)

54
00:02:20,788 --> 00:02:22,387
(Playing the role of a delusional patient)

55
00:02:22,388 --> 00:02:23,427
(He puts on a different face for different projects.)

56
00:02:23,428 --> 00:02:25,188
(Playing the role of a crazy shaman)

57
00:02:25,488 --> 00:02:28,058
(A psychopathic doctor)

58
00:02:28,298 --> 00:02:30,728
(A sleazy government agent)

59
00:02:31,068 --> 00:02:33,668
(The most sought-after actor on the rise)

60
00:02:33,768 --> 00:02:36,538
(Actor Roh Jae Won)

61
00:02:36,738 --> 00:02:38,337
Nice to meet you. Hello.

62
00:02:38,338 --> 00:02:39,477
- Brother. It's been a while.
- Have you seen my works?

63
00:02:39,478 --> 00:02:41,478
Of course. Is this the first time we're meeting?

64
00:02:41,608 --> 00:02:43,378
I've seen you once.

65
00:02:43,548 --> 00:02:44,877
- Right? At an awards ceremony?
- But...

66
00:02:44,878 --> 00:02:46,238
- slightly...
- Where did we meet?

67
00:02:46,478 --> 00:02:49,347
No. We met at the COVID-19 testing clinic.

68
00:02:49,348 --> 00:02:51,288
- Really?
- I saw you by chance.

69
00:02:51,388 --> 00:02:53,888
But back then, I was in college.

70
00:02:54,158 --> 00:02:55,187
- Really?
- Yes.

71
00:02:55,188 --> 00:02:56,657
- We met at the testing clinic?
- Yes.

72
00:02:56,658 --> 00:02:59,157
- You got the test done together?
- Yes. We got it done together.

73
00:02:59,158 --> 00:03:00,928
I was in college back then.

74
00:03:01,528 --> 00:03:03,428
- I knew who you were.
- Right.

75
00:03:03,598 --> 00:03:06,468
I thought it'd be weird if I didn't say hello.

76
00:03:06,598 --> 00:03:08,537
- I said hello before I realized it.
- You said hello?

77
00:03:08,538 --> 00:03:10,708
I did. When you saw me, you did this.

78
00:03:11,638 --> 00:03:13,737
- You weren't sure if you knew me.
- Right.

79
00:03:13,738 --> 00:03:15,237
- That was your reaction.
- Then did I leave?

80
00:03:15,238 --> 00:03:16,607
- You should talk to him up close.
- Okay.

81
00:03:16,608 --> 00:03:18,568
- I can't believe we met before.
- Come this way.

82
00:03:18,608 --> 00:03:20,218
- At the clinic...
- Jae Won.

83
00:03:20,318 --> 00:03:21,958
- Let's sit down first.
- Let's sit down.

84
00:03:22,078 --> 00:03:23,488
Actually,

85
00:03:23,618 --> 00:03:25,217
Yeon Seok mentioned you guys last week.

86
00:03:25,218 --> 00:03:28,687
He said that your movie was going to premiere soon.

87
00:03:28,688 --> 00:03:30,157
- I got the intel.
- He told me that...

88
00:03:30,158 --> 00:03:31,627
you were going to star on our show.

89
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:33,108
I was super arrogant about the intel.

90
00:03:33,158 --> 00:03:34,998
(Acting arrogant)

91
00:03:35,558 --> 00:03:37,027
- He was so arrogant.
- I...

92
00:03:37,028 --> 00:03:38,127
- You're joining us this week.
- Yes.

93
00:03:38,128 --> 00:03:39,467
- I said I played them like a pro.
- You thought we'd be here.

94
00:03:39,468 --> 00:03:41,398
- I played them like a pro.
- But I was wrong.

95
00:03:41,868 --> 00:03:44,267
(The real professionals are finally here.)

96
00:03:44,268 --> 00:03:46,707
It's been so long, Yo Han.

97
00:03:46,708 --> 00:03:48,284
- You've been well, right?
- I've been well.

98
00:03:48,308 --> 00:03:49,308
You look even better now.

99
00:03:49,309 --> 00:03:51,208
Why didn't you invite me to your wedding?

100
00:03:51,548 --> 00:03:52,648
We had a simple wedding.

101
00:03:52,748 --> 00:03:53,947
Why didn't you invite me?

102
00:03:53,948 --> 00:03:55,047
We had a simple wedding with just our families.

103
00:03:55,048 --> 00:03:56,417
Actually, he texted me.

104
00:03:56,418 --> 00:03:58,617
- Right.
- He congratulated me...

105
00:03:58,618 --> 00:04:00,817
and told me to invite me to the wedding.

106
00:04:00,818 --> 00:04:02,287
We only invited our families.

107
00:04:02,288 --> 00:04:03,327
Great.

108
00:04:03,328 --> 00:04:04,757
So you guys invited only your families, right?

109
00:04:04,758 --> 00:04:07,078
Yes. We wouldn't invite some fake families to our wedding.

110
00:04:08,558 --> 00:04:11,667
You know what? This trend started with Jong Kook.

111
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:15,967
Having private weddings has become a trend among celebrities.

112
00:04:15,968 --> 00:04:18,937
A lot of people hold a small, family-only wedding.

113
00:04:18,938 --> 00:04:20,608
- That's right.
- Yes.

114
00:04:20,738 --> 00:04:24,077
I really thought that I had met you, Jae Won.

115
00:04:24,078 --> 00:04:25,577
It turned out we met...

116
00:04:25,578 --> 00:04:27,247
- At the COVID-19 testing clinic.
- Right.

117
00:04:27,248 --> 00:04:28,517
How long has it been? Was that...

118
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:31,147
- It was 4 or 5 years ago.
- in 2020?

119
00:04:31,148 --> 00:04:33,157
It was around Hakdong Station.

120
00:04:33,158 --> 00:04:35,557
- He even remembers the clinic.
- Around Hakdong Station.

121
00:04:35,558 --> 00:04:36,758
Yes.

122
00:04:37,028 --> 00:04:38,388
- The medical clinic?
- Yes.

123
00:04:38,958 --> 00:04:40,697
Back then, we couldn't go to the theaters.

124
00:04:40,698 --> 00:04:42,667
- Right. It hit movie theaters hard.
- Gosh, that wasn't the worst of it.

125
00:04:42,668 --> 00:04:44,127
Back then, movie theaters were...

126
00:04:44,128 --> 00:04:45,467
- going through a dry spell.
- That's right.

127
00:04:45,468 --> 00:04:46,737
Things have improved now.

128
00:04:46,738 --> 00:04:48,037
- Movie theaters...
- Some sold ten million tickets.

129
00:04:48,038 --> 00:04:49,767
- The industry is picking up now.
- Things are picking up now.

130
00:04:49,768 --> 00:04:51,807
Yes. And your movie, "Tazza," will be released now.

131
00:04:51,808 --> 00:04:52,877
- At last.
- Yes.

132
00:04:52,878 --> 00:04:54,877
- When will it be released?
- On September 23.

133
00:04:54,878 --> 00:04:56,607
("Tazza" is in theaters now.)

134
00:04:56,608 --> 00:04:59,317
Jae Won, your recent projects...

135
00:04:59,318 --> 00:05:01,647
have been performing well.

136
00:05:01,648 --> 00:05:03,517
- Right.
- Seriously.

137
00:05:03,518 --> 00:05:05,387
You're in all of successful projects these days.

138
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:06,588
- Right.
- You really are.

139
00:05:06,758 --> 00:05:10,887
So you guys filmed "Tazza" together.

140
00:05:10,888 --> 00:05:12,757
In terms of the series, is this...

141
00:05:12,758 --> 00:05:13,827
This is the finale of the series.

142
00:05:13,828 --> 00:05:14,958
- It's the finale?
- Yes.

143
00:05:15,358 --> 00:05:16,967
This movie is about the inferiority complex...

144
00:05:16,968 --> 00:05:19,898
and revenge of two friends.

145
00:05:20,438 --> 00:05:21,468
What's this?

146
00:05:21,838 --> 00:05:23,807
(The two of them used to be close friends...)

147
00:05:23,808 --> 00:05:25,878
(ever since they were in school, )

148
00:05:27,278 --> 00:05:30,848
(but became the devil who tried to bring each other down.)

149
00:05:31,508 --> 00:05:32,648
Hey, Park Tae.

150
00:05:32,918 --> 00:05:35,077
(The twisted inferiority complex...)

151
00:05:35,078 --> 00:05:37,688
(ruined their friendship.)

152
00:05:38,148 --> 00:05:40,087
(Jang Tae Young, born under a lucky star)

153
00:05:40,088 --> 00:05:41,957
(Park Tae Young, born under a bad sign)

154
00:05:41,958 --> 00:05:43,687
(This time, it's cards, not hwatu.)

155
00:05:43,688 --> 00:05:45,628
(The stakes will be higher.)

156
00:05:46,128 --> 00:05:48,758
(The grand finale of the "Tazza" series)

157
00:05:50,228 --> 00:05:52,227
("Tazza: The Song of Beelzebub")

158
00:05:52,228 --> 00:05:53,637
The previous ones were about hwatu.

159
00:05:53,638 --> 00:05:55,097
- It's about hold 'em.
- This one is about card games.

160
00:05:55,098 --> 00:05:56,468
- Yes.
- I didn't know that.

161
00:05:56,638 --> 00:05:59,107
I bet you had to learn some card tricks for the movie.

162
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:03,248
Yes. We practiced a lot and took lessons.

163
00:06:03,808 --> 00:06:04,877
By the time this episode airs,

164
00:06:04,878 --> 00:06:07,117
your movie would already have been released.

165
00:06:07,118 --> 00:06:08,477
- Really?
- I see.

166
00:06:08,478 --> 00:06:10,687
People promote their projects midway now.

167
00:06:10,688 --> 00:06:13,318
I heard a lot of people watched the movie already during Chuseok.

168
00:06:13,718 --> 00:06:16,027
So many people seem to love our movie.

169
00:06:16,028 --> 00:06:18,787
- Right.
- I'd like to thank them again.

170
00:06:18,788 --> 00:06:20,298
(Thanking the audience in advance)

171
00:06:20,398 --> 00:06:21,497
You're good.

172
00:06:21,498 --> 00:06:22,928
- Gosh, it's a hit.
- Yes.

173
00:06:22,998 --> 00:06:24,797
The Korean movie industry...

174
00:06:24,798 --> 00:06:26,597
- is picking up now.
- That's great.

175
00:06:26,598 --> 00:06:28,567
It'd be nice if the whole industry thrived.

176
00:06:28,568 --> 00:06:31,107
We're at the Incheon Munhak Stadium. Which one of you...

177
00:06:31,108 --> 00:06:32,937
- Who has ties to Incheon?
- Do you guys have ties to Incheon?

178
00:06:32,938 --> 00:06:33,938
It's not you, Yo Han. Is it?

179
00:06:33,939 --> 00:06:35,207
- Both of us...
- We're both from here.

180
00:06:35,208 --> 00:06:36,307
- Really? Incheon?
- Yes.

181
00:06:36,308 --> 00:06:37,977
I didn't know you were from Incheon, Yo Han.

182
00:06:37,978 --> 00:06:39,278
- You too, Jae Won?
- Yes.

183
00:06:39,718 --> 00:06:40,817
Which part of Incheon?

184
00:06:40,818 --> 00:06:44,447
- I grew up in Seo-gu.
- Seo-gu.

185
00:06:44,448 --> 00:06:45,448
- What about you, Yo Han?
- Yo Han?

186
00:06:45,449 --> 00:06:47,858
- I'm from Namdong-gu.
- Namdong-gu.

187
00:06:48,388 --> 00:06:50,727
- There are many famous spots here.
- That's right.

188
00:06:50,728 --> 00:06:53,627
Yes. Could you introduce a few in Namdong-gu?

189
00:06:53,628 --> 00:06:55,188
(Recommend famous spots in Namdong-gu.)

190
00:06:55,228 --> 00:06:57,727
It's around Incheon Culture and Arts Center.

191
00:06:57,728 --> 00:06:58,928
There's an Outback Steakhouse.

192
00:06:59,598 --> 00:07:01,167
(An unexpected famous spot)

193
00:07:01,168 --> 00:07:02,968
- I love Outback Steakhouse.
- Yo Han... Yes.

194
00:07:03,068 --> 00:07:05,607
And this is a famous spot for the locals.

195
00:07:05,608 --> 00:07:06,937
- Right here.
- Yes.

196
00:07:06,938 --> 00:07:08,938
- Right.
- We played against Portugal here.

197
00:07:09,078 --> 00:07:10,078
That's right.

198
00:07:10,079 --> 00:07:12,177
- It was held here.
- It was crazy here.

199
00:07:12,178 --> 00:07:13,217
Did you watch the game?

200
00:07:13,218 --> 00:07:14,317
I had to watch it over the fence.

201
00:07:14,318 --> 00:07:16,617
Everyone wore the Be the Reds shirt.

202
00:07:16,618 --> 00:07:18,148
It was red just like our dress code.

203
00:07:18,488 --> 00:07:19,848
Traffic was completely gridlocked.

204
00:07:19,958 --> 00:07:21,017
- It was crazy.
- Yes.

205
00:07:21,018 --> 00:07:23,927
How old were you in 2002, Jae Won?

206
00:07:23,928 --> 00:07:25,997
- In 2002... I was born in 1993.
- He was born in 1993.

207
00:07:25,998 --> 00:07:29,127
- Were you in elementary school?
- Yes, I was in second grade.

208
00:07:29,128 --> 00:07:31,327
Second grade? You don't remember the games, right?

209
00:07:31,328 --> 00:07:32,997
- No, I remember them.
- You do?

210
00:07:32,998 --> 00:07:34,168
Yes.

211
00:07:34,198 --> 00:07:36,907
I remember that Korea lost to Germany.

212
00:07:36,908 --> 00:07:38,228
Just talk about the games we won.

213
00:07:39,478 --> 00:07:40,777
- Right. Yes.
- There are...

214
00:07:40,778 --> 00:07:42,477
- Just talk about the games we won.
- There are many good memories.

215
00:07:42,478 --> 00:07:45,038
- Why mention the game we lost?
- He takes good care of Jae Won.

216
00:07:45,148 --> 00:07:48,047
Well, that was the most memorable game to me.

217
00:07:48,048 --> 00:07:49,277
- I wanted us to win.
- We would've advanced to the final.

218
00:07:49,278 --> 00:07:50,317
Yes.

219
00:07:50,318 --> 00:07:53,087
Anyway, they were born and raised...

220
00:07:53,088 --> 00:07:55,057
here in Incheon.

221
00:07:55,058 --> 00:07:56,527
- Let's check it out.
- Let's go...

222
00:07:56,528 --> 00:07:58,448
- Let's go.
- and find our first Whenever Guest.

223
00:07:59,658 --> 00:08:01,928
All right. Our first Whenever Guest is Lee Jung Min.

224
00:08:02,358 --> 00:08:06,037
"On weekdays, we find a way to navigate around the gridlock."

225
00:08:06,038 --> 00:08:07,597
"On our days off,"

226
00:08:07,598 --> 00:08:09,879
"we're sky-blue sheriffs who guard the roads in Incheon."

227
00:08:10,408 --> 00:08:12,307
"We've voluntarily given up weekends and national holidays..."

228
00:08:12,308 --> 00:08:14,207
"to be on the road."

229
00:08:14,208 --> 00:08:15,937
"So we need a lot of energy."

230
00:08:15,938 --> 00:08:18,378
"If you ever find yourselves in Incheon, give us a call."

231
00:08:18,648 --> 00:08:20,817
Are they traffic police officers?

232
00:08:20,818 --> 00:08:22,987
- They must be.
- They sound like police officers.

233
00:08:22,988 --> 00:08:24,247
- Yes.
- They do, right?

234
00:08:24,248 --> 00:08:25,518
- Yes.
- Right.

235
00:08:25,918 --> 00:08:26,918
Where is it?

236
00:08:27,588 --> 00:08:28,618
Namdong-gu.

237
00:08:29,158 --> 00:08:30,287
Yes, right.

238
00:08:30,288 --> 00:08:32,087
- Namchon-dong.
- Namchon-dong.

239
00:08:32,088 --> 00:08:33,397
(The Namdong-gu local doesn't feel confident.)

240
00:08:33,398 --> 00:08:34,727
I need to look it up.

241
00:08:34,728 --> 00:08:35,728
(Embarrassed)

242
00:08:35,858 --> 00:08:37,167
I'm getting the sense that you haven't been here for a while.

243
00:08:37,168 --> 00:08:38,527
- Yo Han.
- I don't know where it is...

244
00:08:38,528 --> 00:08:39,967
just by looking at the address.

245
00:08:39,968 --> 00:08:41,037
- You don't?
- No.

246
00:08:41,038 --> 00:08:42,238
I'm going to look it up.

247
00:08:43,868 --> 00:08:45,237
Hold on. Can we take a bus there?

248
00:08:45,238 --> 00:08:46,877
(GPS Byun is on too.)

249
00:08:46,878 --> 00:08:48,007
(GPS Roh is on too.)

250
00:08:48,008 --> 00:08:50,547
- It's okay. The number is 512.
- Let me see.

251
00:08:50,548 --> 00:08:52,448
Are you all looking it up on the map?

252
00:08:52,748 --> 00:08:54,917
Yeon Seok already looked it up. You guys don't have to look it up.

253
00:08:54,918 --> 00:08:56,047
I can just do this.

254
00:08:56,048 --> 00:08:57,848
It's nice to have help.

255
00:08:58,218 --> 00:09:00,788
- On the map, it looks like...
- I see. Here...

256
00:09:01,458 --> 00:09:03,257
We can take Bus Four to get there.

257
00:09:03,258 --> 00:09:04,788
- Bus Four?
- Yes.

258
00:09:05,288 --> 00:09:07,097
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

259
00:09:07,098 --> 00:09:08,357
(They head to the bus stop nearby.)

260
00:09:08,358 --> 00:09:10,397
- You've been well, right?
- Yes. Gosh.

261
00:09:10,398 --> 00:09:11,897
Aren't you going to start filming a drama soon?

262
00:09:11,898 --> 00:09:13,098
- Yes.
- Which college...

263
00:09:13,268 --> 00:09:16,167
The one I filmed with Hyun Jin...

264
00:09:16,168 --> 00:09:17,468
will premiere next month.

265
00:09:18,368 --> 00:09:20,554
My gosh. You're always working. You don't take a break.

266
00:09:20,578 --> 00:09:22,338
- You don't take a break either.
- I don't.

267
00:09:22,538 --> 00:09:24,678
But you're on variety shows too.

268
00:09:25,248 --> 00:09:26,448
But you got married.

269
00:09:26,548 --> 00:09:28,117
- Right.
- Yes.

270
00:09:28,118 --> 00:09:29,864
- I'm older than him.
- Are you guys the same age?

271
00:09:29,888 --> 00:09:31,848
- He's older than me.
- I'm older than him.

272
00:09:32,048 --> 00:09:33,557
But he has more life experience than me now.

273
00:09:33,558 --> 00:09:34,758
- Right.
- Yes.

274
00:09:34,858 --> 00:09:36,957
Yo Han and I would've worn our hair in a topknot...

275
00:09:36,958 --> 00:09:38,327
if this were back in the past.

276
00:09:38,328 --> 00:09:40,527
- Your hair would've been braided.
- Right.

277
00:09:40,528 --> 00:09:41,957
- I couldn't wear it in a topknot.
- Right.

278
00:09:41,958 --> 00:09:42,997
(Two older men with a bachelor with braided hair)

279
00:09:42,998 --> 00:09:44,068
Let's go this way.

280
00:09:44,498 --> 00:09:46,167
- Have you watched our show?
- Yes.

281
00:09:46,168 --> 00:09:47,168
(They keep chatting.)

282
00:09:47,438 --> 00:09:48,498
Are you good at games?

283
00:09:49,068 --> 00:09:50,367
I don't think I'm as good as you.

284
00:09:50,368 --> 00:09:52,807
It's crazy how determined you are...

285
00:09:52,808 --> 00:09:53,878
about these games.

286
00:09:55,508 --> 00:09:56,778
You even got a superpower.

287
00:09:56,908 --> 00:09:59,647
You know what? See it for yourself.

288
00:09:59,648 --> 00:10:01,454
- Does that happen to everyone?
- You become determined.

289
00:10:01,478 --> 00:10:03,078
I bet you'll be more determined than me.

290
00:10:03,218 --> 00:10:05,387
I'm serious. You can see...

291
00:10:05,388 --> 00:10:08,557
our Whenever Guests desperately hoping we succeed.

292
00:10:08,558 --> 00:10:11,157
I'm sure that's a lot of pressure.

293
00:10:11,158 --> 00:10:12,158
- That sense of pressure...
- That's...

294
00:10:12,159 --> 00:10:13,627
Where do you live now?

295
00:10:13,628 --> 00:10:14,797
I still live here.

296
00:10:14,798 --> 00:10:16,467
- You still live here?
- Yes.

297
00:10:16,468 --> 00:10:18,097
(Jae Won still lives in Incheon.)

298
00:10:18,098 --> 00:10:19,327
My family still lives here.

299
00:10:19,328 --> 00:10:21,268
- Everyone lives here.
- And so do I. Yes.

300
00:10:22,038 --> 00:10:23,108
Bus Four comes here.

301
00:10:23,738 --> 00:10:24,938
- This is the bus stop.
- Yes.

302
00:10:25,938 --> 00:10:27,238
When will Bus Four come?

303
00:10:27,938 --> 00:10:29,547
It said earlier that we had to wait 14 minutes.

304
00:10:29,548 --> 00:10:30,777
- Fourteen minutes?
- Yes. Now...

305
00:10:30,778 --> 00:10:31,877
We have to wait ten minutes.

306
00:10:31,878 --> 00:10:33,547
Eleven minutes.

307
00:10:33,548 --> 00:10:34,977
It's cool in the shade.

308
00:10:34,978 --> 00:10:37,048
Yes. It's cool as long as we stay in the shade.

309
00:10:37,918 --> 00:10:40,388
My gosh. That's not cool.

310
00:10:41,488 --> 00:10:42,658
Oh, that?

311
00:10:43,188 --> 00:10:44,188
(Trash thrown onto the roof of the bus stop)

312
00:10:44,189 --> 00:10:46,898
Did they end up on the roof from one of our games?

313
00:10:47,228 --> 00:10:48,327
- Those bottles...
- Like this game.

314
00:10:48,328 --> 00:10:50,488
They just threw away the bottles after finishing them.

315
00:10:50,868 --> 00:10:53,137
They just threw the bottles away when the bus came.

316
00:10:53,138 --> 00:10:54,874
(They threw the bottles high up, making it difficult to clean up.)

317
00:10:54,898 --> 00:10:57,038
- Should we get them down?
- Should we do that?

318
00:10:57,108 --> 00:10:58,937
- Are you tall enough?
- Wait.

319
00:10:58,938 --> 00:11:00,238
Carry me on your shoulders.

320
00:11:02,478 --> 00:11:03,478
Hey.

321
00:11:03,748 --> 00:11:05,954
- I can easily get them down then.
- Let's play rock-paper-scissors.

322
00:11:05,978 --> 00:11:06,978
- The loser has to do it.
- Let's do that.

323
00:11:06,979 --> 00:11:08,347
- The loser has to get the bottles.
- No.

324
00:11:08,348 --> 00:11:10,387
- The winner gets the shoulder ride.
- Okay.

325
00:11:10,388 --> 00:11:11,947
- That's right. It's the winner.
- Okay.

326
00:11:11,948 --> 00:11:14,187
- Rock-paper-scissors.
- Rock-paper-scissors.

327
00:11:14,188 --> 00:11:15,788
(Lost, lost, won, won)

328
00:11:16,328 --> 00:11:17,387
- We'll have to give them a lift.
- Okay.

329
00:11:17,388 --> 00:11:18,988
- The winner has to do it.
- I knew it.

330
00:11:19,158 --> 00:11:21,027
Doesn't it make more sense for us to go on your shoulders?

331
00:11:21,028 --> 00:11:22,997
You're too heavy to get a shoulder ride.

332
00:11:22,998 --> 00:11:24,528
Then Yo Han should get the ride.

333
00:11:24,868 --> 00:11:26,997
- He seems pretty heavy too.
- I...

334
00:11:26,998 --> 00:11:27,998
Right. I'm a bit heavy.

335
00:11:27,999 --> 00:11:29,537
The three of us can give you a lift.

336
00:11:29,538 --> 00:11:30,707
- All right. Let's try that.
- Yes.

337
00:11:30,708 --> 00:11:31,737
Yo Han, you have to do it.

338
00:11:31,738 --> 00:11:33,177
(Model Citizens of Incheon set out.)

339
00:11:33,178 --> 00:11:34,237
How should we lift him up?

340
00:11:34,238 --> 00:11:36,638
- Let's give him a boost.
- No. He should step on our palms.

341
00:11:36,708 --> 00:11:38,207
- Step on your palms?
- We can't lift him with our arms?

342
00:11:38,208 --> 00:11:39,347
Let's try that first.

343
00:11:39,348 --> 00:11:40,478
That's not going to work.

344
00:11:40,748 --> 00:11:42,228
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

345
00:11:42,548 --> 00:11:44,748
- It's going to work.
- He got it.

346
00:11:44,918 --> 00:11:46,048
There you go. Well done.

347
00:11:47,518 --> 00:11:49,087
- You got it.
- Nicely done.

348
00:11:49,088 --> 00:11:51,157
(Model Citizens of Incheon clean up perfectly.)

349
00:11:51,158 --> 00:11:52,327
(The leader finishes up the job.)

350
00:11:52,328 --> 00:11:54,958
- This isn't right. Seriously.
- That was fun.

351
00:11:55,398 --> 00:11:57,667
I'm not sure if whoever threw out the bottles...

352
00:11:57,668 --> 00:11:59,638
- will watch our show.
- Right.

353
00:12:00,398 --> 00:12:03,007
You shouldn't throw out trash like that.

354
00:12:03,008 --> 00:12:04,008
Come on.

355
00:12:04,438 --> 00:12:05,537
- So...
- We did a good deed.

356
00:12:05,538 --> 00:12:06,737
- How could they clean this up?
- Right.

357
00:12:06,738 --> 00:12:07,808
My beloved city.

358
00:12:08,638 --> 00:12:10,118
- I think that's the bus.
- Bus Four.

359
00:12:10,278 --> 00:12:11,808
- Right.
- Bus Four.

360
00:12:12,578 --> 00:12:14,117
- You got this?
- Yes. I got it.

361
00:12:14,118 --> 00:12:15,148
I pay for the bus rides.

362
00:12:15,348 --> 00:12:16,587
(They move toward to the bus stop.)

363
00:12:16,588 --> 00:12:18,588
- We don't pay individually?
- I pay for everyone.

364
00:12:19,318 --> 00:12:20,918
- He has the transportation card.
- Yes.

365
00:12:21,288 --> 00:12:22,487
- This doesn't cost much.
- Wait.

366
00:12:22,488 --> 00:12:23,758
- It's just passing by.
- Wait.

367
00:12:23,958 --> 00:12:25,688
(Screaming)

368
00:12:26,428 --> 00:12:27,458
What was that?

369
00:12:30,598 --> 00:12:32,438
Do buses not stop if drivers don't see anyone?

370
00:12:33,098 --> 00:12:34,637
(The bus driver didn't see them and drove past them.)

371
00:12:34,638 --> 00:12:35,668
Wait.

372
00:12:37,508 --> 00:12:38,908
Is this normal?

373
00:12:40,438 --> 00:12:41,438
The bus just left like that?

374
00:12:41,439 --> 00:12:42,719
(The three of them are shocked.)

375
00:12:43,248 --> 00:12:44,547
- I guess you had to wave.
- What?

376
00:12:44,548 --> 00:12:46,224
- I guess you had to wave.
- You had to be in the front.

377
00:12:46,248 --> 00:12:48,547
(They were taking their sweet time behind the bus stop and missed it.)

378
00:12:48,548 --> 00:12:49,868
Hold on. We had to be there by...

379
00:12:50,048 --> 00:12:51,087
I had no idea.

380
00:12:51,088 --> 00:12:52,287
We have to wave at the bus...

381
00:12:52,288 --> 00:12:54,217
if we want to get on the bus in Incheon?

382
00:12:54,218 --> 00:12:56,357
- I should've...
- Earlier, the lady...

383
00:12:56,358 --> 00:12:57,758
We should've sat down here earlier.

384
00:12:58,258 --> 00:12:59,387
We had no idea.

385
00:12:59,388 --> 00:13:00,897
(Pickup Point)

386
00:13:00,898 --> 00:13:02,127
- Let's sit down.
- Wait.

387
00:13:02,128 --> 00:13:03,527
(The pickup point is further ahead than expected.)

388
00:13:03,528 --> 00:13:05,897
- Jae Won.
- I'm flustered.

389
00:13:05,898 --> 00:13:07,098
What about Bus Five?

390
00:13:07,368 --> 00:13:08,897
Bus Five is good too.

391
00:13:08,898 --> 00:13:10,507
But it will take 33 minutes.

392
00:13:10,508 --> 00:13:12,837
- That takes too long?
- Yes.

393
00:13:12,838 --> 00:13:15,377
We have to be there by 11:30am.

394
00:13:15,378 --> 00:13:17,448
- Then...
- Here's what I noticed.

395
00:13:17,878 --> 00:13:21,718
The drivers only stop if you wave them down fiercely.

396
00:13:22,418 --> 00:13:23,517
We have no choice then.

397
00:13:23,518 --> 00:13:25,118
(They end up waiting for the bus again.)

398
00:13:25,348 --> 00:13:26,988
- It will be here in five minutes.
- Yes.

399
00:13:28,718 --> 00:13:30,687
I landed in Korea yesterday.

400
00:13:30,688 --> 00:13:32,969
- Really? From where?
- We went on a late honeymoon trip.

401
00:13:33,528 --> 00:13:35,498
You were on your honeymoon? Where did you go?

402
00:13:36,198 --> 00:13:37,927
We went to a warm country. We went to Hawaii.

403
00:13:37,928 --> 00:13:38,928
Hawaii, yes.

404
00:13:38,929 --> 00:13:41,797
We went to San Francisco because she grew up there.

405
00:13:41,798 --> 00:13:43,007
I bet it was great.

406
00:13:43,008 --> 00:13:44,467
- It was great.
- Right.

407
00:13:44,468 --> 00:13:46,628
I wouldn't have come back if it weren't for this show.

408
00:13:47,278 --> 00:13:48,377
Thank you.

409
00:13:48,378 --> 00:13:49,878
- Wait. Not yet.
- Is it here?

410
00:13:50,148 --> 00:13:51,207
No.

411
00:13:51,208 --> 00:13:52,708
- we're traumatized.
- Right.

412
00:13:53,318 --> 00:13:55,047
- Whenever we see a bus...
- We have to open our arms up.

413
00:13:55,048 --> 00:13:56,048
Whenever we see a bus...

414
00:13:56,049 --> 00:13:57,148
It's at the previous stop.

415
00:13:58,188 --> 00:13:59,317
Okay.

416
00:13:59,318 --> 00:14:00,487
(They'll stand at the pickup point in advance.)

417
00:14:00,488 --> 00:14:02,918
- My gosh, seriously.
- Let's move up now.

418
00:14:03,488 --> 00:14:05,157
(Actively flagging down the driver)

419
00:14:05,158 --> 00:14:07,104
- The bus is coming toward us.
- Yes. What a relief.

420
00:14:07,128 --> 00:14:08,228
That's a relief.

421
00:14:09,458 --> 00:14:11,598
- Hello.
- Thank you.

422
00:14:11,828 --> 00:14:13,238
- Hello.
- Hello.

423
00:14:13,838 --> 00:14:16,407
My gosh. This is nice.

424
00:14:16,408 --> 00:14:17,807
- We got on an empty bus.
- I wouldn't have felt this great...

425
00:14:17,808 --> 00:14:19,667
if I got on the bus easily.

426
00:14:19,668 --> 00:14:21,408
- Right.
- Exactly.

427
00:14:21,908 --> 00:14:23,124
Do you often use public transportation?

428
00:14:23,148 --> 00:14:25,407
- I always take the bus and subway.
- Really?

429
00:14:25,408 --> 00:14:27,317
- Really?
- Yes.

430
00:14:27,318 --> 00:14:29,678
But why didn't you tell us we had to flag down the drivers?

431
00:14:30,088 --> 00:14:32,487
- Pardon?
- Why didn't you let us know?

432
00:14:32,488 --> 00:14:34,758
- I...
- I didn't know...

433
00:14:34,858 --> 00:14:37,387
- it'd just drive past us. No.
- You didn't know?

434
00:14:37,388 --> 00:14:38,628
I didn't know.

435
00:14:39,628 --> 00:14:40,697
Living here...

436
00:14:40,698 --> 00:14:42,098
There will be announcements, right?

437
00:14:42,698 --> 00:14:43,827
The announcements?

438
00:14:43,828 --> 00:14:44,828
(He's nervous to take the bus for the first time in Incheon.)

439
00:14:44,829 --> 00:14:46,429
What if getting off the bus is hard too?

440
00:14:47,668 --> 00:14:49,807
- Wait. Where do we need to get off?
- How many stops do we need to go?

441
00:14:49,808 --> 00:14:51,867
We got on the bus, so we need to get off at the right stop.

442
00:14:51,868 --> 00:14:52,907
- Okay.
- Where is it?

443
00:14:52,908 --> 00:14:54,107
I've been monitoring the route.

444
00:14:54,108 --> 00:14:57,807
- Okay. Namchon-dong Entrance.
- Namchon-dong.

445
00:14:57,808 --> 00:14:58,948
Namchon-dong.

446
00:15:00,548 --> 00:15:03,348
When did you move out of Incheon?

447
00:15:03,548 --> 00:15:04,788
I lived here until high school.

448
00:15:05,488 --> 00:15:07,288
I went to school here up through high school.

449
00:15:07,618 --> 00:15:09,058
- Up through high school?
- Yes.

450
00:15:09,118 --> 00:15:10,228
You too, Jae Won?

451
00:15:10,428 --> 00:15:13,398
I went to school here up through middle school.

452
00:15:13,658 --> 00:15:16,328
I went to high school in Anyang.

453
00:15:17,868 --> 00:15:19,467
- Was it Anyang Arts High School?
- Yes.

454
00:15:19,468 --> 00:15:21,338
You went to Anyang Arts High School.

455
00:15:22,238 --> 00:15:23,738
What were you like in high school?

456
00:15:24,138 --> 00:15:25,138
During your school years?

457
00:15:25,139 --> 00:15:26,877
I had so much fun in school.

458
00:15:26,878 --> 00:15:28,184
- I went to an arts high school.
- Anyang Arts High School.

459
00:15:28,208 --> 00:15:29,507
- Anyang Arts High School.
- Anyang Arts High School.

460
00:15:29,508 --> 00:15:31,978
- They all majored in Acting.
- Right.

461
00:15:32,108 --> 00:15:33,448
Were you quiet in school?

462
00:15:33,648 --> 00:15:37,087
I didn't think that...

463
00:15:37,088 --> 00:15:38,487
I was quiet in school.

464
00:15:38,488 --> 00:15:39,858
I had fun.

465
00:15:40,518 --> 00:15:41,887
- I was playful.
- Really?

466
00:15:41,888 --> 00:15:44,057
There's a subtle streak of mischief...

467
00:15:44,058 --> 00:15:45,527
all over your face.

468
00:15:45,528 --> 00:15:47,858
- Right. I can be quite mischievous.
- Yes.

469
00:15:48,258 --> 00:15:51,068
But only around people I'm close to.

470
00:15:51,268 --> 00:15:52,728
- You need time to open up.
- Yes.

471
00:15:52,868 --> 00:15:54,537
He's playful around his close friends.

472
00:15:54,538 --> 00:15:56,507
I've gotten close to Yo Han.

473
00:15:56,508 --> 00:15:58,608
Yo Han...

474
00:15:59,108 --> 00:16:01,478
(Looking around)

475
00:16:02,778 --> 00:16:04,218
Is this the Culture and Arts Center?

476
00:16:04,808 --> 00:16:06,207
- Yes.
- Isn't the bus terminal here?

477
00:16:06,208 --> 00:16:07,347
Right, the bus terminal.

478
00:16:07,348 --> 00:16:09,077
The bus terminal is here? You know where we are now?

479
00:16:09,078 --> 00:16:10,817
- And...
- Right. There's a bus terminal.

480
00:16:10,818 --> 00:16:13,488
I performed in a play at the Culture and Arts Center...

481
00:16:13,858 --> 00:16:16,658
when I was in middle school for the first time.

482
00:16:16,858 --> 00:16:17,858
Ever since then...

483
00:16:17,859 --> 00:16:20,404
- That's where your dream started?
- I dreamed of becoming an actor.

484
00:16:20,428 --> 00:16:22,357
- Right.
- There's an open plaza...

485
00:16:22,358 --> 00:16:24,228
in front of the department store.

486
00:16:24,868 --> 00:16:26,068
I used to breakdance there.

487
00:16:26,368 --> 00:16:27,537
- You used to breakdance?
- Yes.

488
00:16:27,538 --> 00:16:28,818
I used to do the windmill there.

489
00:16:29,938 --> 00:16:31,508
This is the birthplace of my dreams.

490
00:16:32,508 --> 00:16:33,777
This is the main street, right?

491
00:16:33,778 --> 00:16:36,477
- It used to be the busiest area...
- Right?

492
00:16:36,478 --> 00:16:37,998
- in Incheon back then.
- Michuhol-gu.

493
00:16:38,308 --> 00:16:39,847
What was Incheon like when you were growing up?

494
00:16:39,848 --> 00:16:41,418
Incheon was nicknamed the Devildom.

495
00:16:42,018 --> 00:16:45,247
(The legend of Incheon by an Incheon native)

496
00:16:45,248 --> 00:16:47,318
There's a produce and fish market around here.

497
00:16:47,688 --> 00:16:49,057
People fight with napa cabbages and radishes.

498
00:16:49,058 --> 00:16:50,698
- Why?
- That's how it's done in Incheon.

499
00:16:51,728 --> 00:16:54,598
(Bragging about his hometown with dignity)

500
00:16:54,858 --> 00:16:56,138
With napa cabbages and radishes?

501
00:16:56,298 --> 00:16:58,867
- But people here are very friendly.
- Of course.

502
00:16:58,868 --> 00:17:00,197
They're very affectionate.

503
00:17:00,198 --> 00:17:01,437
That's their way of expressing affection.

504
00:17:01,438 --> 00:17:03,238
- With napa cabbages and radishes.
- Isn't...

505
00:17:03,338 --> 00:17:05,438
Jemulpo High School famous here?

506
00:17:05,708 --> 00:17:06,737
- It's a famous school.
- It's a famous school.

507
00:17:06,738 --> 00:17:08,237
- Jemulpo High School.
- The school is located...

508
00:17:08,238 --> 00:17:10,308
- in the east of Incheon.
- I see.

509
00:17:10,648 --> 00:17:13,277
Are vibes different between eastern...

510
00:17:13,278 --> 00:17:14,417
- and western Incheon?
- So...

511
00:17:14,418 --> 00:17:16,017
We call them the East Side and the West Side.

512
00:17:16,018 --> 00:17:17,188
When you go there,

513
00:17:18,148 --> 00:17:19,747
older guys take your money as soon as you get off the bus.

514
00:17:19,748 --> 00:17:22,148
(Older guys take your money as soon as you get off the bus.)

515
00:17:22,458 --> 00:17:25,457
I always had to hide my pocket money in my socks.

516
00:17:25,458 --> 00:17:26,458
(Incheon was quite different back in the day.)

517
00:17:26,459 --> 00:17:27,497
- You know what?
- There's nothing I can do.

518
00:17:27,498 --> 00:17:28,657
That's the neighborhood...

519
00:17:28,658 --> 00:17:30,428
- I grew up in.
- You know what?

520
00:17:30,598 --> 00:17:32,097
I grew up in Seoul.

521
00:17:32,098 --> 00:17:34,197
- Which part of Seoul?
- I grew up in Suyu-ri.

522
00:17:34,198 --> 00:17:36,814
- That's a rough neighborhood. Yes.
- I saw a lot of bullies growing up.

523
00:17:36,838 --> 00:17:38,007
When we were in school,

524
00:17:38,008 --> 00:17:39,437
- They were everywhere.
- there were so many bullies.

525
00:17:39,438 --> 00:17:40,577
- There were so many bullies.
- Yes.

526
00:17:40,578 --> 00:17:42,307
- Seriously.
- And that was the era.

527
00:17:42,308 --> 00:17:44,747
We had to be competitive and fierce to survive.

528
00:17:44,748 --> 00:17:46,184
- We had to be.
- We had to be competitive.

529
00:17:46,208 --> 00:17:47,977
- We need to survive today's games.
- I...

530
00:17:47,978 --> 00:17:49,217
- I'm going to do my best.
- Yes.

531
00:17:49,218 --> 00:17:50,548
I'll do my best.

532
00:17:51,448 --> 00:17:52,888
- Do we need to get off?
- Shall we?

533
00:17:53,048 --> 00:17:54,587
- Gosh.
- Thank you.

534
00:17:54,588 --> 00:17:56,257
- Thank you.
- Tag the card.

535
00:17:56,258 --> 00:17:57,688
Okay. Thank you.

536
00:17:59,958 --> 00:18:02,728
My gosh. Where are we going?

537
00:18:04,328 --> 00:18:05,667
It looks like we're going to the wilderness.

538
00:18:05,668 --> 00:18:08,767
- Right. I don't see anything here.
- It looks empty here.

539
00:18:08,768 --> 00:18:09,967
(Sky-blue sheriffs are in a place like this?)

540
00:18:09,968 --> 00:18:13,167
Wait. Could it be the Best Driver Association?

541
00:18:13,168 --> 00:18:14,477
Could it be that over there?

542
00:18:14,478 --> 00:18:16,177
- Where?
- There's an office.

543
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:17,378
Over there?

544
00:18:17,478 --> 00:18:19,107
- I see.
- That must be it.

545
00:18:19,108 --> 00:18:20,817
On weekends, they...

546
00:18:20,818 --> 00:18:21,977
- Right.
- Yes.

547
00:18:21,978 --> 00:18:23,548
- They volunteer on weekends.
- Yes.

548
00:18:23,848 --> 00:18:24,988
I see.

549
00:18:25,288 --> 00:18:26,988
- "Best Driver Association."
- We're here.

550
00:18:27,288 --> 00:18:28,688
You know what?

551
00:18:28,958 --> 00:18:30,627
- It's here?
- It says, "Council."

552
00:18:30,628 --> 00:18:31,757
"Council."

553
00:18:31,758 --> 00:18:33,157
(Gently knocking on the door)

554
00:18:33,158 --> 00:18:34,898
- Hello.
- Hi.

555
00:18:35,328 --> 00:18:36,328
Hello.

556
00:18:36,329 --> 00:18:37,797
- Hello. Nice to meet you.
- Are you Mr. Lee Jung Min?

557
00:18:37,798 --> 00:18:39,067
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

558
00:18:39,068 --> 00:18:40,637
- My gosh.
- Hello.

559
00:18:40,638 --> 00:18:42,668
- Hello. Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

560
00:18:43,508 --> 00:18:45,608
- Please sit down.
- Okay. This way.

561
00:18:45,738 --> 00:18:46,938
My gosh. Nice to meet you.

562
00:18:47,538 --> 00:18:50,578
(A veteran taxi driver who navigates every corner of Incheon)

563
00:18:50,878 --> 00:18:53,478
(Taxi Driver Lee Jung Min)

564
00:18:53,578 --> 00:18:55,317
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

565
00:18:55,318 --> 00:18:56,917
(They've never been to the office of the Best Driver Association.)

566
00:18:56,918 --> 00:18:59,448
This is the Namdong-gu office...

567
00:18:59,588 --> 00:19:02,318
- of the Best Driver Association.
- Yes.

568
00:19:02,388 --> 00:19:04,328
(Intrigued)

569
00:19:04,888 --> 00:19:06,697
We often go to your alma mater.

570
00:19:06,698 --> 00:19:08,197
- Which one?
- Guwolseo Elementary School.

571
00:19:08,198 --> 00:19:09,398
- Really?
- Yes.

572
00:19:09,968 --> 00:19:12,298
- We... Yes.
- Did you know I was coming?

573
00:19:12,628 --> 00:19:13,768
You knew I was coming today?

574
00:19:13,898 --> 00:19:15,868
I had a gut feeling. You filmed "Tazza 4."

575
00:19:17,038 --> 00:19:18,067
(Locals just get each other.)

576
00:19:18,068 --> 00:19:19,868
- You had a feeling it'd be him.
- Yes.

577
00:19:20,038 --> 00:19:21,638
I was wondering if it would be you guys.

578
00:19:21,978 --> 00:19:23,347
- I see.
- Yes.

579
00:19:23,348 --> 00:19:25,778
- You were right.
- Both of them are from Incheon.

580
00:19:26,348 --> 00:19:27,377
- Yes.
- So...

581
00:19:27,378 --> 00:19:29,988
how long have you worked as a taxi driver?

582
00:19:30,048 --> 00:19:33,788
I became a taxi driver right after my military discharge.

583
00:19:33,918 --> 00:19:35,758
- I became a taxi driver very young.
- Really?

584
00:19:35,888 --> 00:19:37,127
But I didn't work as a taxi driver for a long time.

585
00:19:37,128 --> 00:19:40,198
I drove my taxi for a bit over a year.

586
00:19:40,398 --> 00:19:42,528
I came back to this job in 2000.

587
00:19:42,658 --> 00:19:43,897
- In 2000?
- Yes.

588
00:19:43,898 --> 00:19:45,227
- But still. It's been 26...
- So it's been about 26 years.

589
00:19:45,228 --> 00:19:47,198
- to 27 years now.
- Yes.

590
00:19:47,368 --> 00:19:49,598
So I took a look around the office.

591
00:19:49,698 --> 00:19:51,584
I see that the association is in charge of many duties.

592
00:19:51,608 --> 00:19:53,007
Could you tell us about the duties?

593
00:19:53,008 --> 00:19:55,078
During the morning rush hour,

594
00:19:55,538 --> 00:19:57,047
we keep traffic moving...

595
00:19:57,048 --> 00:19:58,107
- Right.
- at each intersection.

596
00:19:58,108 --> 00:19:59,547
Things can get hectic.

597
00:19:59,548 --> 00:20:01,777
So we work at the intersections to help with traffic duties.

598
00:20:01,778 --> 00:20:03,617
We go to elementary and middle schools...

599
00:20:03,618 --> 00:20:05,987
- For safety.
- to make sure safety.

600
00:20:05,988 --> 00:20:08,094
The largest number of volunteers is deployed at the day of the CSAT.

601
00:20:08,118 --> 00:20:10,134
- On the day of the CSAT.
- On the day of the CSAT.

602
00:20:10,158 --> 00:20:12,727
- On the day of the CSAT, - Right.

603
00:20:12,728 --> 00:20:15,158
All of our members volunteer.

604
00:20:16,128 --> 00:20:18,128
But you don't receive any monetary benefits...

605
00:20:18,468 --> 00:20:21,067
- from the association.
- We don't.

606
00:20:21,068 --> 00:20:23,967
We volunteer on our own initiative.

607
00:20:23,968 --> 00:20:25,037
(It's a volunteer organization without pay.)

608
00:20:25,038 --> 00:20:27,077
We're just a group of volunteers just like me.

609
00:20:27,078 --> 00:20:29,178
A friend of mine said this to me.

610
00:20:29,878 --> 00:20:33,248
"You lived for yourself for the past 50 years."

611
00:20:33,648 --> 00:20:35,547
"Why don't you live a life, helping others..."

612
00:20:35,548 --> 00:20:37,687
"for the remaining years of your life?"

613
00:20:37,688 --> 00:20:40,618
How should I put it? He kept trying to get me to join.

614
00:20:41,788 --> 00:20:43,257
Just like you said,

615
00:20:43,258 --> 00:20:45,027
not any taxi drivers can join this association.

616
00:20:45,028 --> 00:20:46,897
- There are requirements, right?
- Yes.

617
00:20:46,898 --> 00:20:50,298
To join, you must have driven a commercial vehicle...

618
00:20:50,398 --> 00:20:52,518
- for over two years, accident-free.
- Accident-free.

619
00:20:52,828 --> 00:20:55,797
And you can't have a felony record.

620
00:20:55,798 --> 00:20:57,467
- Of course.
- You can't have a criminal record.

621
00:20:57,468 --> 00:20:59,408
- Right. There must be requirements.
- Yes.

622
00:20:59,668 --> 00:21:01,578
- I can see that...
- Yes.

623
00:21:02,208 --> 00:21:03,808
- you're second in line.
- Yes.

624
00:21:04,178 --> 00:21:05,777
- That's the chairman.
- Yes.

625
00:21:05,778 --> 00:21:06,977
- You're the senior vice chairman.
- Yes.

626
00:21:06,978 --> 00:21:08,818
- You're the senior vice chairman.
- Right.

627
00:21:09,948 --> 00:21:11,618
Will you be the chairman next term?

628
00:21:13,248 --> 00:21:14,758
- You're on TV now.
- Right.

629
00:21:15,358 --> 00:21:17,758
You're on TV now.

630
00:21:17,988 --> 00:21:21,058
When you're volunteering, I'm sure some people upset you.

631
00:21:21,358 --> 00:21:22,638
- That happens sometimes.
- Yes.

632
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:24,227
Earlier today, when we were coming here,

633
00:21:24,228 --> 00:21:25,598
we got upset at the bus stop.

634
00:21:25,828 --> 00:21:27,667
- Really?
- Yes. Someone threw out...

635
00:21:27,668 --> 00:21:29,738
two water bottles on the roof of the bus stop.

636
00:21:30,138 --> 00:21:32,838
Yo Han took care of the trash.

637
00:21:32,968 --> 00:21:35,538
People from Namdong-gu have exemplary character.

638
00:21:36,508 --> 00:21:39,677
But Yeon Seok and Jae Won gave him a lift.

639
00:21:39,678 --> 00:21:42,317
(We helped out too.)

640
00:21:42,318 --> 00:21:43,787
I'm sure you encounter unpleasant people...

641
00:21:43,788 --> 00:21:45,817
- when you volunteer.
- Yes. Some curse at us.

642
00:21:45,818 --> 00:21:47,858
- "Who do you think you are?"
- Right.

643
00:21:47,988 --> 00:21:49,217
- They shouldn't do that.
- Seriously.

644
00:21:49,218 --> 00:21:52,528
- Come on. Why, Yeon Seok?
- I know, right?

645
00:21:52,988 --> 00:21:54,528
Me? Wait.

646
00:21:55,458 --> 00:21:57,867
I was a military driver. I follow traffic regulations.

647
00:21:57,868 --> 00:21:58,997
- I was looking for your approval.
- Okay.

648
00:21:58,998 --> 00:22:00,838
I was looking for your approval of my opinion.

649
00:22:00,898 --> 00:22:02,778
Nice to meet you. I was also a military driver.

650
00:22:03,268 --> 00:22:04,748
- This keeps happening.
- That again?

651
00:22:04,968 --> 00:22:06,937
- It keeps happening.
- He talks about himself every week.

652
00:22:06,938 --> 00:22:08,677
- This happened again.
- His time as a military driver,

653
00:22:08,678 --> 00:22:11,608
Sejong University, and his military service in the Air Force.

654
00:22:11,708 --> 00:22:13,148
I wasn't going to talk about myself.

655
00:22:13,208 --> 00:22:15,977
Since Yo Han and Jae Won are joining us today,

656
00:22:15,978 --> 00:22:17,987
I hope we can make it to Round Three.

657
00:22:17,988 --> 00:22:20,588
- You're both from Incheon.
- Right. You're both from Incheon.

658
00:22:20,888 --> 00:22:22,688
- I'll do my best.
- Sounds good.

659
00:22:22,818 --> 00:22:24,658
- We'll give you everything.
- Thank you.

660
00:22:25,758 --> 00:22:27,297
We're starting right away.

661
00:22:27,298 --> 00:22:29,497
- Okay.
- Please open...

662
00:22:29,498 --> 00:22:30,698
the first fortune cookie.

663
00:22:30,968 --> 00:22:31,997
Please read it.

664
00:22:31,998 --> 00:22:34,968
"I'm the Tom Cruise of Incheon when I'm behind the wheel."

665
00:22:35,138 --> 00:22:36,767
"Two pairs of Ray-Ban sunglasses..."

666
00:22:36,768 --> 00:22:38,768
"for me and my close friend, the chairman."

667
00:22:39,538 --> 00:22:42,438
(We're the Tom Cruise of Incheon! Ray-Ban sunglasses)

668
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:44,447
(Amazed)

669
00:22:44,448 --> 00:22:45,577
- Two pairs.
- Sunglasses for the chairman...

670
00:22:45,578 --> 00:22:46,578
and the vice chairman.

671
00:22:46,579 --> 00:22:47,747
(Friendship sunglasses for the leaders)

672
00:22:47,748 --> 00:22:49,388
- They definitely need sunglasses.
- Yes.

673
00:22:49,478 --> 00:22:51,187
(Parking Master)

674
00:22:51,188 --> 00:22:52,987
(They must park...)

675
00:22:52,988 --> 00:22:55,957
(the toy taxi in the parking zone.)

676
00:22:55,958 --> 00:22:59,028
(Round 1: Park 2 out of 4 toy taxis.)

677
00:22:59,288 --> 00:23:00,457
(Park the taxi?)

678
00:23:00,458 --> 00:23:01,798
Is it a miniature taxi?

679
00:23:02,158 --> 00:23:04,368
(Mini taxi cars)

680
00:23:05,298 --> 00:23:06,697
(They must park mini taxi cars...)

681
00:23:06,698 --> 00:23:09,067
We have pro-gamers today.

682
00:23:09,068 --> 00:23:11,168
- Let's try it.
- I doubt we'll be disappointed.

683
00:23:11,368 --> 00:23:15,237
- My goodness. Listen.
- Okay. I'm good at parking.

684
00:23:15,238 --> 00:23:16,407
- It has no power.
- But...

685
00:23:16,408 --> 00:23:18,088
The wheels can't be on the line like this?

686
00:23:18,678 --> 00:23:19,908
- Here too?
- Yes.

687
00:23:20,008 --> 00:23:21,077
(Driving through)

688
00:23:21,078 --> 00:23:22,247
- Right.
- Gosh.

689
00:23:22,248 --> 00:23:23,347
This will be tough.

690
00:23:23,348 --> 00:23:24,648
This one? I see.

691
00:23:25,188 --> 00:23:26,447
- It also rolls.
- You can push it...

692
00:23:26,448 --> 00:23:27,848
or wind up the car. It's up to you.

693
00:23:28,988 --> 00:23:30,217
Pushing it would be better. Right?

694
00:23:30,218 --> 00:23:31,538
- We can just push it too?
- Yes.

695
00:23:31,988 --> 00:23:33,287
I see. We can use different methods.

696
00:23:33,288 --> 00:23:34,528
(He tries winding up the car.)

697
00:23:34,858 --> 00:23:36,258
I see. This is...

698
00:23:37,628 --> 00:23:38,728
It doesn't look easy.

699
00:23:38,928 --> 00:23:40,368
- It won't be easy.
- It's not easy.

700
00:23:40,768 --> 00:23:42,198
With the chairman here...

701
00:23:42,398 --> 00:23:43,467
Oh, no.

702
00:23:43,468 --> 00:23:44,867
(His presence doubles their pressure.)

703
00:23:44,868 --> 00:23:46,907
We have to decide whether to wind up the car or not.

704
00:23:46,908 --> 00:23:48,707
We can just decide that on our own, right? It's up to us.

705
00:23:48,708 --> 00:23:49,778
It's up to you.

706
00:23:49,978 --> 00:23:51,748
(He winds up the car to practice.)

707
00:23:52,248 --> 00:23:53,378
This isn't easy.

708
00:23:53,978 --> 00:23:55,078
You got it.

709
00:23:56,778 --> 00:23:58,647
- See that? He did it.
- Right? Jae Won got it.

710
00:23:58,648 --> 00:24:00,658
- If I start from here...
- I think I can do it.

711
00:24:01,118 --> 00:24:02,157
We can push it too, right?

712
00:24:02,158 --> 00:24:03,628
(Pushing the car)

713
00:24:03,658 --> 00:24:05,157
Pushing it... How is it?

714
00:24:05,158 --> 00:24:07,158
- I think it's better.
- This is...

715
00:24:07,898 --> 00:24:09,398
Should I just push it?

716
00:24:11,668 --> 00:24:12,728
It won't work.

717
00:24:13,098 --> 00:24:14,098
Pushing it...

718
00:24:14,099 --> 00:24:16,699
For the right direction, winding it up is better than pushing it.

719
00:24:18,638 --> 00:24:21,208
Hold on. I should try starting a little farther back.

720
00:24:21,308 --> 00:24:23,038
We've got to succeed.

721
00:24:23,378 --> 00:24:25,248
Let me, a former military driver, try.

722
00:24:27,678 --> 00:24:28,777
The former military driver.

723
00:24:28,778 --> 00:24:30,448
(Sergeant Ahn takes the stage.)

724
00:24:32,348 --> 00:24:33,917
- Isn't that too...
- Come on.

725
00:24:33,918 --> 00:24:35,487
(The military driver is embarrassed.)

726
00:24:35,488 --> 00:24:36,618
Give me a second.

727
00:24:39,488 --> 00:24:41,498
Allow me to practice a little.

728
00:24:44,998 --> 00:24:46,167
(Letting go)

729
00:24:46,168 --> 00:24:47,198
He's got it.

730
00:24:48,798 --> 00:24:49,798
Okay.

731
00:24:52,568 --> 00:24:54,484
- How did I do it?
- I've gotten the hang of it.

732
00:24:54,508 --> 00:24:56,407
It's okay to be gentle.

733
00:24:56,408 --> 00:24:57,507
- The others can push it in.
- Exactly.

734
00:24:57,508 --> 00:24:59,028
- That sounds better.
- It could work.

735
00:24:59,848 --> 00:25:02,047
The wheels of my car...

736
00:25:02,048 --> 00:25:04,888
While keeping the wheels outside of the line,

737
00:25:05,088 --> 00:25:07,118
- Pull it?
- if I pull the car back...

738
00:25:07,888 --> 00:25:09,518
so that...

739
00:25:10,118 --> 00:25:13,158
it's within the circle...

740
00:25:15,758 --> 00:25:17,368
(Parked perfectly)

741
00:25:18,028 --> 00:25:20,167
(Jae Won established a parking theory.)

742
00:25:20,168 --> 00:25:21,437
- Nice.
- You got it.

743
00:25:21,438 --> 00:25:22,738
You got the direction.

744
00:25:24,068 --> 00:25:26,468
(Practicing as taught by Jae Won)

745
00:25:30,108 --> 00:25:31,247
(Parked successfully)

746
00:25:31,248 --> 00:25:33,407
- I did it.
- You've also gotten the hang of it.

747
00:25:33,408 --> 00:25:34,848
That's it. I've got it.

748
00:25:35,048 --> 00:25:36,477
- You have.
- Listen.

749
00:25:36,478 --> 00:25:38,518
I think we can do it if we adjust the distance.

750
00:25:39,388 --> 00:25:40,858
See that?

